    <node id="Spatula">
      <data key="d0">Spatula</data>
      <data key="d1">object</data>
      <data key="d2">The spatula is a versatile kitchen utensil that plays an essential role in various culinary tasks. It is typically characterized by a flat, broad rectangular blade attached to a long handle, which can be made from materials such as metal, plastic, silicone, or wood. Spatulas are commonly used for flipping, spreading, or lifting food items, making them integral to both cooking and serving processes. They are available in a variety of colors, including black, and are designed for ease of use in both preparation and presentation of dishes. Overall, the spatula is considered a staple in kitchens, underscoring its importance in culinary activities.</data>
      <data key="d3">"Can flip;"Used for flipping, spreading, or lifting food;"can be held;"flip;"lift;can be moved;can be used to mix ingredients.";flip;flip";lift;lift";mix";pick_up_once";serve;serve";spread;transfer";used to flip or transfer food items"</data>
      <data key="d4">"N/A";"heat_limitation;"keep_away_from_heat_sources;"should be placed in an appropriate receptacle to avoid confusion;"should_be_used_carefully_with_hot_surfaces;avoid_using_on_non_stick_pans_with_sharp_edges";clean_before_use";if_made_of_plastic;if_sharp_edges,_not_use_on_non-stick_pans";may require confirmation of successful pick-up before movement";not_suitable_for_non-stick_cookware";placement must match the intended receptacle location</data>
      <data key="d5">"N/A"&lt;SEP&gt;"N/A"&lt;SEP&gt;The entity in question, Spatula, is currently unused and stored. The other descriptions provided are labeled as "N/A" and do not offer any additional relevant information.</data>
      <data key="d6">"N/A"&lt;SEP&gt;The spatula is prominently featured in an image, where it is depicted in the lower left corner, resting on a small wooden table towards the left side of the room. Its specific placement is noted to be in the lower-left-middle part of the tabletop, arranged diagonally with the handle tilted upwards while the flat end rests on the counter. Although the initial position of the spatula was on the right counter, the description indicates that it was subsequently moved to the left counter for interaction purposes. This summary captures the spatula's transition from the right counter to its current location on the wooden table, highlighting its significant presence within the space.&lt;SEP&gt;"initially found on the right counter"</data>
      <data key="d7">A spatula is a versatile kitchen utensil used primarily for flipping, spreading, and lifting food items during cooking and serving. Characterized by its flat design and long handle, the spatula enhances ease of use during food preparation. It typically features a broad, flat blade, often rectangular in shape, making it an essential tool for various culinary applications. Spatulas can be made from materials such as plastic, metal, wood, or silicone, catering to different needs in the kitchen.

In one specific instance, a black spatula with a flat end is noted for its positioning in the lower-left-middle part of a table, resting diagonally for convenient accessibility, although it remains unused at this time. Furthermore, an update on the spatula indicates that it can only be picked up once and is now located on the right counter. Additionally, it is highlighted as an object that can be held and moved, emphasizing its practical function in transferring food or substances. Overall, the spatula's design and multifunctionality underline its significance in facilitating a wide range of food-related tasks within the kitchen.</data>
      <data key="d8">chunk-1719a68ee00ddb7af0b3ec1cdd6dd669&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c200ce7eb06ff3e3c2dd1282801f14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3766328c3cde2e0365b9ffc47d9f6bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-169309fedde4a9cb38576d40b2edaa65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b34e0bd973ce36ba976971b3ec8a7a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bbb30025846d31c16ebf72f6b1f6420&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d1f9bba3ce5abf1a1ab4116ebc3d7a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ebb0449f8b1154979b33180229558760&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd717652fd4474e55f4df3f31f73880a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a40a7080f080163a5b021c623248055</data>
