    <node id="Pliers">
      <data key="d0">Pliers</data>
      <data key="d1">object</data>
      <data key="d2">Pliers are a type of hand tool characterized by their two handles and jaws, utilized primarily for gripping and cutting tasks. They are designed to assist in various manual operations, providing a means to hold, twist, pull, or cut objects effectively. The tool's construction facilitates a strong grip on items, making it an essential instrument in numerous crafts and repair activities.</data>
      <data key="d3">"grip;bend;cut"</data>
      <data key="d4">"N/A";"sharp_edges"</data>
      <data key="d5">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d6">The entity in question is Pliers. They are located in the foreground, positioned left of center on the kitchen counter. The descriptions consistently indicate that Pliers are situated on the counter's left side.</data>
      <data key="d7">Pliers are a handheld tool defined by two levers and a gripping mechanism, utilized for gripping, bending, and cutting materials. They are commonly found in various environments, including kitchens, and are specifically located on the counter's left side. Their versatile design allows them to be effective for a range of tasks involving different materials.</data>
