    <node id="Green Apple">
      <data key="d0">Green Apple</data>
      <data key="d1">object</data>
      <data key="d2">Green Apple is a type of fruit that is typically green in color, crisp, and tart. It is recognized for its round shape and is edible, making it a popular choice among fruits. Commonly known for its sweet and tart flavor, the Green Apple is often consumed fresh, adding to its appeal as a refreshing and flavorful snack.</data>
      <data key="d3">"Can be eaten;cut";juiced";sliced;used in cooking;used in cooking and baking;used in cooking";used in cooking."</data>
      <data key="d4">"N/A";"Should be kept away from moisture to avoid spoilage";"Should be kept away from moisture to avoid spoilage."</data>
      <data key="d5">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d6">"On the table towards the front and slightly to the left."&lt;SEP&gt;"On the table towards the front and slightly to the left; left of the gray rock."</data>
      <data key="d7">The Green Apple is a small, smooth fruit characterized by its green skin. Often found in domestic settings, it typically adorns tables, suggesting its use for both consumption and decoration. This round fruit is commonly enjoyed fresh as a snack and is frequently utilized in various culinary dishes, making it a versatile ingredient in the kitchen.</data>
