    <node id="Furniture">
      <data key="d0">Furniture</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Furniture is a general category of objects designed to support various human activities and tasks. This includes items intended for sitting, storing, or supporting purposes. Specifically, furniture encompasses various objects that facilitate activities such as seating or sleeping, serving as fundamental components in both residential and commercial environments.</data>
      <data key="d3">"Can be used to provide comfort, storage, and surfaces for activities.";"N/A";"Supports relaxation and social interaction"</data>
      <data key="d4">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d5">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d6">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d7">Furniture is a broad category that encompasses a variety of items serving functional purposes in living spaces. This includes essential objects such as tables, chairs, sofas, and couches, all of which contribute to both comfort and utility. Additionally, furniture can also refer to specific fixtures like sinks in kitchen or bathroom settings. Overall, furniture plays a crucial role in enhancing the functionality and aesthetic of different environments.</data>
