    <node id="Bicycle">
      <data key="d0">Bicycle</data>
      <data key="d1">object</data>
      <data key="d2">The bicycle is a two-wheeled vehicle designed for recreation or fitness, characterized by its ability to be powered by human pedaling. It typically features a metal frame, handlebars, pedals, two wheels, and a seat to facilitate riding. The descriptions indicate that this particular bicycle has a distinctive appearance, with a red frame and black wheels. Additionally, it may come in variations featuring a combination of black and red, equipped with thin wheels and standard sizing. Overall, the bicycle is valued for its functionality and versatility as a mode of transportation and exercise.</data>
      <data key="d3">"Can be ridden for transportation or physical activity.";"Can be ridden for travel;"Supports personal transportation and exercise";"can be ridden for transportation;"ride;exercise;exercise";recreation";suitable for fitness and recreation.";transport</data>
      <data key="d4">"N/A";"Requires balance;usage may be restricted on certain pathways."</data>
      <data key="d5">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d6">The bicycle is described as distinguishable by its red frame and black tires, positioned near the back wall of a room, adjacent to a gray exercise ball. It is leaning against the wall in the background area, specifically noted to be towards the midground on the far side of the room. Additionally, it is reported to be positioned upright near the left wall of the room. Overall, the bicycle's positioning is consistent throughout the descriptions, emphasizing its location against the wall amid other elements in the room.</data>
      <data key="d7">A bicycle is a human-powered vehicle that consists of two wheels and is typically utilized for transportation or sport. Designed with a red frame and thin black tires, it serves as a means of human transportation and exercise. Bicycles are often used for personal transport and recreation, making them popular for both daily commuting and physical activity. In one context, a bicycle can be observed leaning against a wall, positioned behind an exercise ball, highlighting its role in promoting fitness and recreation.</data>
      <data key="d8">chunk-13d95292d79ecefc8be8a2545b74f251&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8dfff6f8b76245965ff5da952e9b121&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-169309fedde4a9cb38576d40b2edaa65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a40a7080f080163a5b021c623248055&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7cf82458894c268eb3ff8bd5554fcf7</data>
      <data key="d9">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d10">1772715946</data>
    </node>
